---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout current="/" description="Richard J. Allen is an operations and customer-success leader with experience in people management, SaaS support, process improvement, training, reporting, and cross-functional execution.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Operations · Customer Success · Process Improvement · People Leadership</div>
    <h1>Helping people, processes, customers, and operations work better together.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I’m Richard Allen, an operations and customer-success leader based in Oregon. I’ve managed customer-support and technical-support teams, led process and documentation programs, built management reporting, coordinated software and service changes, trained teams and customers, and worked across operations ranging from SaaS support to workforce and supply operations.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/case-studies/">View selected work</a><a class="button secondary" href="/resume/">View résumé</a><a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Career impact at a glance</div><h2>Management scope and operational proof.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Selected examples from people leadership, process improvement, workforce operations, and reporting.</p></div>
    <div class="stats-grid">
      <article class="stat-card teal"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">32</span></div><div class="metric-label">Customer Support and Technical Support representatives managed after promotion to Customer Support Manager at HawkSoft</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card blue"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">125+</span></div><div class="metric-label">SOPs in the year-long OED modernization program, including 25+ legacy procedures inventoried and updated</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card gold"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">400+</span></div><div class="metric-label">workforce position records managed across multiple Oregon Health Authority divisions</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card violet"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">20+</span></div><div class="metric-label">recurring and ad-hoc workforce reports maintained for leadership</div></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Choose the most relevant path</div><h2>Experience organized by the job you are hiring for.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Each path emphasizes the same verified career history through a different recruiter lens.</p></div>
    <div class="grid two value-grid">
      <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">01</div><h3>Operations & people leadership</h3><p>Promoted from Team Lead to Customer Support Manager at HawkSoft, managing 32 support and technical-support representatives. Additional experience includes coaching, hiring, performance, workflow coverage, reporting, cross-functional coordination, workforce operations, and earlier warehouse/supply management.</p><a href="/operations-leadership/">Operations & leadership →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">02</div><h3>Customer success & SaaS support</h3><p>Customer relationships, technical-support leadership, escalations, training, software adoption, migrations, year-long Customer Journey leadership, release support, and customer-experience improvement.</p><a href="/customer-success/">Customer success experience →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">03</div><h3>Process improvement & documentation</h3><p>Led a year-long SOP modernization and governance program across roughly 10 functional groups, updating 25+ legacy procedures and building a centralized library that ultimately encompassed 125+ SOPs.</p><a href="/process-improvement/">Process improvement work →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">04</div><h3>Implementation & enablement</h3><p>Customer and hosted-service migrations, major software-change readiness, advance communication, launch coverage, functional testing, product documentation, training, onboarding, and coordination between technical and customer-facing teams.</p><a href="/implementation-enablement/">Implementation & enablement →</a></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section project-work-home"><div class="container">
    <div class="project-teaser">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow light">Also available for selected project work</div>
        <h2>Need an important process documented clearly?</h2>
        <p>I take on selected short-term projects involving SOP creation and cleanup, workflow documentation, training/onboarding guides, support-operations procedures, and documentation governance. This remains a secondary project-work lane alongside my primary search for the right long-term role.</p>
        <div class="service-chips"><span>SOPs</span><span>Workflow documentation</span><span>Training guides</span><span>Support procedures</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="project-actions"><a class="button button-light" href="/project-work/">View project services</a><a class="text-link-light" href="/contact/">Discuss a project →</a></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <div class="callout"><strong>Leadership beyond the workplace.</strong> Volunteer hospital chaplaincy, community administration, emergency-preparedness coordination, mentoring, and service work reinforce the same habits I value professionally: listening, organizing, communicating clearly, and helping people move through real-world needs. <a href="/community-leadership/">See community & volunteer leadership →</a></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
